Z||000000||glava2876||04-18-2001||05:42 PM||||I want to start by thanking everyone for all of the help so far in getting my Fiero running after 10 years of hibernation. At this point it turns over freely, but only sarts with by dumping fuel in the TB and then stops. No fuel, but what is the best sequence for trouble shooting. After the engine stalls, it sounds like the fuel pump runs a little then stops after reaching pressure? Fuel filter is new. Under the injector wiring looked a little rusty, so I hit it with WD-40 to soak. Can I take the injector appart and clean it? If so where can I get an exploded view -I don't have a manual yet. Or what other things should I check? Thanks again, Glen    ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-18-2001||06:14 PM||||Hey Glen!<BR>When the engine is turning over, you should see fuel squirting from the injector (TBI 2M4)...<BR>If not, there is only a screen around the injector...<BR>Try running the fuel into a bucket to ensure the fuel is pumped to the injector...<BR>If you do have fuel at the injector, but it won't start,try another injector, or ECM output is shot...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
